 "version": 1,
 "title": "Pop Pluck Riff",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: the bright, bouncing sequenced riff of early-80s synth-pop: a short, glassy pluck running up and down a chord, echoing behind itself. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: Clock 1/16 \u2192 Sequencer (eight notes of a chord and its octave) \u2192 one oscillator, saw and pulse mixed, through the Ladder filter; a short envelope plucks both the filter and the VCA on every step. A touch of Drive brightens it; a Delay a dotted eighth behind (at this tempo) makes the echoes fall between the notes; a little Reverb. Hold a key around middle C and the riff plays from it.\n\nTweak: the step knobs (it's a melody: change it), the envelope's DECAY, the filter's CUTOFF and RESONANCE, the delay's TIME and FEEDBACK, TEMPO.",
